Each stage contains separate squares made from matches. No matches are shared.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm]
\foreach \x in {0,3,4.3,7,8.3,9.6}{\draw[draw=black,line width=0.6pt] (\x,0) rectangle +(1,1);}
\path (0.5,-0.6) node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black]{Stage 1};
\path (4.15,-0.6) node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black]{Stage 2};
\path (8.8,-0.6) node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black]{Stage 3};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Describe the relationship between the stage number and the number of matches using multiplication. Explain how this description finds the number of matches at stage $8$ directly.
